# .dockerignore — keep Docker build context small for cargo-chef multi-stage builds.
#
# Source: 03-RESEARCH.md §"Code Examples §7" + 03-CONTEXT.md (.dockerignore is mandatory).
# Without this file, every COPY scoops ~500 MB of target/ — see RESEARCH §Pitfall 8.
#
# IMPORTANT: this list MUST stay in sync with the in-tree .gitignore for the items
# below (target/, results/, report/, *.swp, .DS_Store) so the Docker build context
# matches the tracked workspace; everything else is Docker-specific.
#
# Files that MUST NOT appear here (the Dockerfiles + cargo-chef rely on them):
#   Cargo.toml          ← workspace + per-crate manifests
#   Cargo.lock          ← reproducible exact-version pins
#   crates/             ← all source
#   rust-toolchain.toml ← rustc version pin (1.91)
#   .cargo/config.toml  ← rustflags for native (Phase 1); Dockerfiles override via ENV RUSTFLAGS
#   crates/*/build.rs   ← scoped under crates/, never excluded
#
# We intentionally keep *.md (CLAUDE.md, README.md) inside the build context: their
# presence is harmless and BuildKit's dep-cache invalidation behaves better when the
# context shape is consistent across builds.

# Build artifacts (huge — most important entry)
target/
**/target/

# Git, planning, IDE
.git/
.gitignore
.planning/
.cargo-ok
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Docs that don't affect the build
docs/

# Test/bench results (generated, not part of source)
results/
report/

# Misc
.DS_Store
**/*.rs.bk
